{
  "info": {
    "name": "Masar — Search & Ride-Request Flow E2E",
    "description": "End-to-end verification of the driver↔passenger search and ride-request flow against a local dev server (base_url env var).\n\nChain: passenger+driver login → my-trips baseline → driver publishes a trip → passenger search finds it (filters + no-leak) → passenger posts a ride request → driver board lists it → driver accepts (creates a NEW trip + confirmed booking) → driver my-trips shows the accepted trip (default and ?status=published) → accept-created trip is publicly searchable → booking visible to both sides → accept-with-trip_id attach path → negatives (re-accept 409, passenger accept 403) → regression: type_of_trip \"once\" accepted (was 422) → full-trip edge (accepted booking fills the vehicle → status full; hidden from ?status=published) → accepted offers list embeds the current trip summary (single call, no N+1).\n\nIncludes fix-verification assertions: the accept response's trip.available_seats/status must match the database (stale-response fix), and type_of_trip \"once\" must be accepted (validator fix).\n\nNOTE: expects a clean trips/ride_requests/bookings state — if the driver already has a published trip on the same route, accept attaches to it instead of creating a new trip (by design) and the \"brand-NEW trip\" assertion fails. Reset the flow tables (trips, trip_seats, trip_stops, trip_attributes, bookings, ride_requests, request_offers, ratings, delay_events, notifications, recent_searches, audit_logs) before re-running.\n\nRun: postman collection run search_flow_e2e.json -e environments/local-e2e.json\nCredentials come from Main Server/seed-mock.ts (Test@1234).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "const DAY = 86400000;",
          "const now = Date.now();",
          "if (!pm.environment.get('search_date')) {",
          "  const dayA = 3 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 7);",
          "  pm.environment.set('search_date', new Date(now + DAY).toISOString().slice(0, 10));",
          "  pm.environment.set('trip_a_departure', new Date(now + dayA * DAY).toISOString().slice(0, 10) + 'T08:00:00+03:00');",
          "  pm.environment.set('request_1_origin_time', new Date(now + (dayA - 1) * DAY).toISOString());",
          "  pm.environment.set('request_3_origin_time', new Date(now + (dayA + 1) * DAY).toISOString().slice(0, 10) + 'T10:00:00+03:00');",
          "  pm.environment.set('request_4_origin_time', new Date(now + (dayA + 2) * DAY).toISOString().slice(0, 10) + 'T11:00:00+03:00');",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0 Setup",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login Passenger (Rana)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"phone\": \"+962780000001\",\n  \"password\": \"Test@1234\",\n  \"role\": \"passenger\"\n}" },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/auth/login"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Passenger login returns 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Login returns access_token', () => pm.expect(j.access_token).to.be.a('string').and.to.have.lengthOf.at.least(20));",
                  "pm.environment.set('passenger_token', j.access_token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Login Driver (Omar)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"phone\": \"+962790000001\",\n  \"password\": \"Test@1234\",\n  \"role\": \"driver\"\n}" },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/auth/login"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Driver login returns 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Login returns access_token', () => pm.expect(j.access_token).to.be.a('string').and.to.have.lengthOf.at.least(20));",
                  "pm.environment.set('driver_token', j.access_token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Driver - my-trips baseline (before publish)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{driver_token}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/trips/driver/my-trips"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('my-trips baseline returns 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('trips is an array', () => pm.expect(j.trips).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "pm.environment.set('driver_trip_ids_before', JSON.stringify((j.trips || []).map(t => t.trip_id)));",
                  "console.log('[flow] driver trips before this run:', (j.trips || []).length);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1 Driver publishes a trip",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Driver - Create Trip A (Amman→Irbid)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{driver_token}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"origin_city\": \"Amman\",\n  \"origin_area\": \"Abdali\",\n  \"destination_city\": \"Irbid\",\n  \"destination_area\": \"University Street\",\n  \"departure_time\": \"{{trip_a_departure}}\",\n  \"type_of_trip\": \"once\",\n  \"fare_per_seat\": \"15.50\",\n  \"allowed_type\": \"all\",\n  \"seats\": [\n    { \"seat_number\": 1, \"type\": \"driver\" },\n    { \"seat_number\": 2, \"type\": \"available\" },\n    { \"seat_number\": 3, \"type\": \"available\" },\n    { \"seat_number\": 4, \"type\": \"unavailable\" },\n    { \"seat_number\": 5, \"type\": \"unavailable\" }\n  ],\n  \"instructions\": [\"No smoking please\"],\n  \"additional_instructions\": \"Bring water\",\n  \"stops\": [\n    { \"name\": \"Jerash\", \"city\": \"Jerash\", \"lat\": \"32.2800\", \"lng\": \"35.8900\", \"stop_type\": \"both\", \"stop_order\": 1 }\n  ]\n}" },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/trips"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Trip created (201)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Response has trip_id', () => pm.expect(j.trip_id).to.be.a('string').and.to.have.lengthOf.at.least(10));",
                  "pm.test('Trip is published', () => pm.expect(j.status).to.eql('published'));",
                  "pm.test('Available seats = 2', () => pm.expect(Number(j.available_seats)).to.eql(2));",
                  "pm.environment.set('trip_a_id', j.trip_id);",
                  "console.log('[flow] trip_a_id =', j.trip_id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2 Passenger search",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Passenger - Search finds the driver's trip",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{passenger_token}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/trips/search/available?origin_city=Amman&destination_city=Irbid&date={{search_date}}&seats=1"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Search returns 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Response has trips array', () => pm.expect(j.trips).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "const found = (j.trips || []).filter(t => t.id === pm.environment.get('trip_a_id'));",
                  "pm.test(\"Driver-created trip is found by passenger search\", () => pm.expect(found.length).to.eql(1));",
                  "if (found.length) {",
                  "  const t = found[0];",
                  "  pm.test('Found trip is published', () => pm.expect(t.status).to.eql('published'));",
                  "  pm.test('Driver profile attached', () => { pm.expect(t.driver).to.be.an('object'); pm.expect(t.driver.full_name).to.eql('Omar Al-Rashid'); });",
                  "  pm.test('Vehicle attached', () => pm.expect(t.vehicle).to.be.an('object'));",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Passenger - Search with filters (time+vehicle+gender+seats)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{passenger_token}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/trips/search/available?origin_city=Amman&destination_city=Irbid&date={{search_date}}&time_from=06:00&time_to=23:00&vehicle_type=sedan&gender_preference=all&seats=1"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Filtered search returns 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Trip still found with time/vehicle/gender/seats filters', () => pm.expect((j.trips || []).map(t => t.id)).to.include(pm.environment.get('trip_a_id')));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Passenger - Search other route (no leakage)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{passenger_token}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/trips/search/available?origin_city=Zarqa&destination_city=Amman&date={{search_date}}&seats=1"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Search returns 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Trip A not returned for a different route', () => pm.expect((j.trips || []).map(t => t.id)).to.not.include(pm.environment.get('trip_a_id')));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3 Ride request → driver accept → my-trips (NEW trip)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Passenger - Create ride request (Amman→Dead Sea)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{passenger_token}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"origin_city\": \"Amman\",\n  \"origin_place\": \"Sweifieh\",\n  \"origin_lat\": 31.9520,\n  \"origin_lng\": 35.8620,\n  \"destination_city\": \"Dead Sea\",\n  \"destination_place\": \"Amman Beach\",\n  \"destination_lat\": 31.5874,\n  \"destination_lng\": 35.5569,\n  \"origin_time\": \"{{request_1_origin_time}}\",\n  \"seats_needed\": 1,\n  \"max_budget\": 8,\n  \"note\": \"E2E flow verification request\"\n}" },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/ride-requests"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Ride request created (201)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('ride_request payload returned', () => { pm.expect(j.ride_request).to.be.an('object'); pm.expect(j.ride_request.id).to.be.a('string'); });",
                  "pm.test('Status is open', () => pm.expect(j.ride_request.status).to.eql('open'));",
                  "pm.environment.set('request_1_id', j.ride_request.id);",
                  "pm.environment.set('passenger_id', j.ride_request.passenger_id);",
                  "console.log('[flow] request_1_id =', j.ride_request.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Passenger - Matches for the request",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{passenger_token}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/ride-requests/{{request_1_id}}/matches"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Matches returns 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('matches is an array', () => pm.expect(j.matches).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "pm.test('each match exposes trip_id / departure_time / available_seats', () => (j.matches || []).forEach(m => { pm.expect(m.trip_id).to.be.a('string'); pm.expect(m.departure_time).to.be.a('string'); pm.expect(Number(m.available_seats)).to.be.a('number'); }));",
                  "console.warn('[DESIGN NOTE] /matches does NOT filter by route — it returns every published trip with seats inside a ±24h/+48h time window, ranked by route+time+seat+gender score. Route relevance affects ranking only.');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Driver - Request board lists the new request",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{driver_token}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/ride-requests?limit=50"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Board returns 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('data is an array', () => pm.expect(j.data).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "const row = (j.data || []).filter(r => r.id === pm.environment.get('request_1_id'));",
                  "pm.test('New request is visible on the driver board', () => pm.expect(row.length).to.eql(1));",
                  "if (row.length) { pm.test('Listed as open', () => pm.expect(row[0].status).to.eql('open')); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Driver - Accept request (creates a NEW trip)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{driver_token}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{}" },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/ride-requests/{{request_1_id}}/accept"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Accept succeeds (200/201)', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 201]));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('trip block returned', () => pm.expect(j.trip).to.be.an('object'));",
                  "const before = JSON.parse(pm.environment.get('driver_trip_ids_before') || '[]');",
                  "const isNewTrip = before.indexOf(j.trip.id) === -1;",
                  "pm.environment.set('accept_created_new', String(isNewTrip));",
                  "pm.test('Accept created a brand-NEW trip (driver had no same-route published trip)', () => pm.expect(isNewTrip).to.eql(true));",
                  "pm.test('New trip route matches the request (Amman→Dead Sea)', () => { pm.expect(j.trip.origin_city).to.eql('Amman'); pm.expect(j.trip.destination_city).to.eql('Dead Sea'); });",
                  "pm.test('New trip is published', () => pm.expect(j.trip.status).to.eql('published'));",
                  "pm.environment.set('accept_reported_seats', String(Number(j.trip.available_seats)));",
                  "console.log('[fix check] accept response available_seats =', j.trip.available_seats, '— must equal the my-trips value (stale-response fix).');",
                  "pm.test('Booking is confirmed on the new trip', () => { pm.expect(j.booking).to.be.an('object'); pm.expect(j.booking.status).to.eql('confirmed'); pm.expect(j.booking.trip_id).to.eql(j.trip.id); pm.expect(Number(j.booking.seats_booked)).to.eql(1); });",
                  "pm.test('Booking belongs to the requesting passenger', () => pm.expect(j.booking.passenger_id).to.eql(pm.environment.get('passenger_id')));",
                  "pm.test('Accept records an accepted offer', () => { pm.expect(j.offer).to.be.an('object'); pm.expect(j.offer.status).to.eql('accepted'); });",
                  "pm.environment.set('trip_b_id', j.trip.id);",
                  "pm.environment.set('booking_1_id', j.booking.id);",
                  "console.log('[flow] trip_b_id =', j.trip.id, '| booking_1_id =', j.booking.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Driver - my-trips includes the accept-created trip (default)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{driver_token}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/trips/driver/my-trips"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('my-trips returns 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('trips is an array', () => pm.expect(j.trips).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "const ids = (j.trips || []).map(t => t.trip_id);",
                  "pm.test('ACCEPT-CREATED trip appears in my-trips', () => pm.expect(ids).to.include(pm.environment.get('trip_b_id')));",
                  "pm.test('Driver-created trip also appears', () => pm.expect(ids).to.include(pm.environment.get('trip_a_id')));",
                  "const b = (j.trips || []).find(t => t.trip_id === pm.environment.get('trip_b_id'));",
                  "if (b) {",
                  "  const reported = Number(pm.environment.get('accept_reported_seats'));",
                  "  pm.test('accept response seat count matches my-trips DB truth (' + reported + ') — stale-response fix verified', () => pm.expect(reported).to.eql(Number(b.available_seats)));",
                  "  pm.test('Accept-created trip is published in my-trips', () => pm.expect(b.status).to.eql('published'));",
                  "  pm.test('seats and waypoints includes present', () => { pm.expect(b.seats).to.be.an('array'); pm.expect(b.waypoints).to.be.an('array'); });",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Driver - my-trips?status=published includes it too",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{driver_token}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/trips/driver/my-trips?status=published"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Filtered my-trips returns 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('ACCEPT-CREATED trip appears in ?status=published my-trips', () => pm.expect((j.trips || []).map(t => t.trip_id)).to.include(pm.environment.get('trip_b_id')));",
                  "pm.test('All returned trips are published', () => (j.trips || []).forEach(t => pm.expect(t.status).to.eql('published')));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Passenger - Search now finds the accept-created trip",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{passenger_token}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/trips/search/available?origin_city=Amman&destination_city=Dead%20Sea&date={{search_date}}&seats=1"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Search returns 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Accept-created trip is publicly searchable', () => pm.expect((j.trips || []).map(t => t.id)).to.include(pm.environment.get('trip_b_id')));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Passenger - My bookings shows the confirmed booking",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{passenger_token}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/bookings?status=confirmed&limit=50"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('My bookings returns 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "const row = (j.data || []).find(b => b.id === pm.environment.get('booking_1_id'));",
                  "pm.test('Confirmed booking visible to passenger', () => pm.expect(row).to.be.an('object'));",
                  "if (row) {",
                  "  pm.test('Booking confirmed on the accept-created trip (Amman→Dead Sea)', () => { pm.expect(row.status).to.eql('confirmed'); pm.expect(row.trip.origin.city).to.eql('Amman'); pm.expect(row.trip.destination.city).to.eql('Dead Sea'); });",
                  "}",
                  "console.warn('[CONTRACT NOTE] passenger booking rows (serializePassengerDetail) have NO trip_id field — only a nested trip object. Driver booking rows (serializeListRow) DO expose trip_id. Clients must read the trip differently per role.');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Driver - Driver bookings shows the booking",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{driver_token}}", "type": "string" }] },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/driver/bookings?status=confirmed&limit=50"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Driver bookings returns 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Confirmed booking visible to driver', () => pm.expect((j.data || []).map(b => b.id)).to.include(pm.environment.get('booking_1_id')));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4 Accept with explicit trip_id (attach path)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Passenger - Create ride request 2 (Amman→Irbid)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
